3. Calls upon all parties to ensure full, safe, unhindered and sustained humanitarian access to all parts of Syria, including to the north-west and to all persons in need without discrimination, including through the expansion of cross-line deliveries from Damascus across conflict lines, in full respect for Syria’s sovereignty and territorial integrity and in coordination with the Syrian authorities, United Nations humanitarian actors and other relevant parties, in accordance with international humanitarian law and the United Nations guiding principles of humanitarian emergency assistance, and encourages the United Nations and its humanitarian partners to strengthen cross-line operations and early recovery projects in coordination with relevant parties;
4. Requests the Secretary-General to ensure that the cross-border mechanism is used in full transparency and in strict compliance with the United Nations guiding principles of humanitarian emergency assistance, and to ensure that cross-border and cross-line deliveries are complementary and respond to assessed humanitarian needs, including by strengthening cross-line operations, where feasible, with a view to a phased transition from cross-border to cross-line delivery, consistent with the temporary and exceptional nature of the cross-border mechanism;
